            <div xml:id="d983">

                <pb facs="1068" n="1056" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg1056"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Cotracil/9–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-28T15:00:00+01:00">September 28,
                            1945—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 28—11:59 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10087. Delsec 79 from the Secretary. Reference urtel 7740, September 8. On the
                    question of terminating military government in the Bolzano area I consider that
                    it is important that there be no change just at this time in the administration
                    of this area since the settlement with Italy is still before the Council Foreign
                    Ministers. Please request the War Department to defer any arrangement for
                    withdrawal until I can review the matter after the termination of this
                    Conference. [Byrnes.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
